---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleHero from '../../components/articles/ArticleHero.astro';
import ArticleContent from '../../components/articles/ArticleContent.astro';
import ArticleStats from '../../components/articles/ArticleStats.astro';
import ArticleContactForm from '../../components/articles/ArticleContactForm.astro';
import ArticleTestimonials from '../../components/articles/ArticleTestimonials.astro';
import ArticleMap from '../../components/articles/ArticleMap.astro';

const title = "Adrienne D. Logeman | Ann Arbor Personal Injury Attorney";
const description = "Attorney Adrienne D. Logeman represents injured clients throughout Michigan. Learn about her experience and dedication to taking cases others won't.";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <ArticleHero />
  <ArticleContent>
    <h2>Meet Adrienne D. Logeman</h2>

    <p>Ms. Logeman is a practicing lawyer since 2002 in Ann Arbor, Michigan. She received her bachelors from University of Michigan in bio-psychology/neuroscience. She received her law degree from Michigan State Law School.</p>

    <blockquote>
      <p>She also served on the Board of Directors for Eversight and volunteers with Donate for Life.</p>
    </blockquote>

    <p>For more than a decade, Adrienne has lectured for ICLE and Michigan Association for Justice on automobile litigation and no-fault matters. She specializes in complex no-fault issues including priority of carriers, home modifications, health insurance priorities, spinal cord and TBI cases and overlapping probate issues. She handles matters in State and Federal Court.</p>

    <p>She is a member of the Michigan Association for Justice, the Washtenaw County Bar Association and Institute of Continuing Legal Education.</p>

    <figure>
      <img src="https://pagesmith-cdn.com/881ce63c/images/693a57355b27c6a8906778c1_Michigan-No-Fault-Automobile-Cases-Law-and-Practice-3-220.webp" alt="Michigan No-Fault Automobile Cases Law and Practice" />
    </figure>

    <p>Currently, she is one of the co-authors of <em>A No-Fault Automobile Law and Practice in Michigan</em>.</p>

    <p>She is a frequent guest speaker for the Institute of Continuing Legal Education and Michigan Association for Justice and Washtenaw County Bar Association, CMSA and Washtenaw County Probate Training.</p>

    <h3>Education</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Michigan State University College of Law</strong>, East Lansing, Michigan
        <ul>
          <li>J.D. - 2001</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li><strong>University of Michigan - Ann Arbor</strong>, Ann Arbor, Michigan
        <ul>
          <li>B.S. - 1998</li>
          <li>Honors: <em>cum laude</em></li>
          <li>Major: Bio-psychology (neuroscience emphasis)</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Bar Admissions</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Michigan, 2002</li>
      <li>U.S. District Court Eastern District of Michigan, 2002</li>
      <li>U.S. District Court Western District of Michigan, 2002</li>
      <li>U.S. Court of Appeals 6th Circuit, 2002</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Professional Associations</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Washtenaw Co. Bar Association, Member, 2002 to Present</li>
      <li>Michigan Bar Association, Member, 2002 to Present</li>
      <li>Michigan Trial Lawyers Association, Member, 2002 to Present</li>
      <li>Member of the Michigan Association for Justice</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Published Works</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Co-Authors of <em>No-Fault Automobile Law and Practice in Michigan</em></li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Classes &amp; Seminars</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>ICLE No Fault Institute Serve as moderator, and on planning seminar, 2014, 2015, 2016, 2018</li>
      <li>Michigan Association of Justice Speaker, 2015 to Present</li>
      <li>RINC Speaker, 2014 to 2014</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Pro-Bono Activities</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Ronald McDonald House – Volunteer, 1996 to 1999</li>
      <li>Organ Donation Events – Volunteer with events, fund-raising and community outreach with various organizations (Buddy Day, Donate for Life, Eye Banks, Lions Club), 2010 to Present</li>
      <li>Ann Arbor Lion Club – Member, 2010 to Present</li>
      <li>Midwest Eye Bank – Board of Director member for a non-profit entity, Treasurer, 2010 to 2016</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Languages</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>English</li>
    </ul>
  </ArticleContent>
  <ArticleStats />
  <ArticleContactForm />
  <ArticleTestimonials />
  <ArticleMap />
</BaseLayout>
